\newpage
\begin{verbatim}
%
% TRANSFORMATION TSubjOK
< m1: CLAUSE{CLAUSErec1}
            [ mu1,
              subjrel/T1,
              mu2,
              predrel/VERBP{VERBPrec1}
                     [ mu3,
                       head/VERB{VERBrec1}[mu5],
                       mu6
                     ],
              mu4
            ]
>

< m : CLAUSE{CLAUSErec1}
            [ mu1,
              subjrel/T1,
              mu2,
              predrel/VERBP{VERBPrec1}
                     [ mu3,
                       head/VERB{VERBrec1}[mu5],
                       mu6
                     ],
              mu4 
            ]
>

   MATCHCONDITIONS
      <
       m1: ( EXIST (mu2, [auxrel/I1::VERB{VERBrec2}[mu7]]) )
           OR
           ( CLAUSErec1.voice <> Passive  AND
             ( (NOT CLAUSErec1.thetavp IN [vp010, vp012]) OR
                VERBrec1.Caseassigner <> false )
           )
       m : ( EXIST (mu2, [auxrel/I1::VERB{VERBrec2}[mu7]]) )
           OR
           ( CLAUSErec1.voice <> Passive  AND
             ( (NOT CLAUSErec1.thetavp IN [vp010, vp012]) OR
                VERBrec1.Caseassigner <> false )
           )
         I1: VERBrec2.subc = modalverb
      >

      COMP
         <
          C1: true
          A1: @
         >
      DECOMP
         <
          C1: true
          A1: @
         >
&

\end{verbatim}
\newpage
\begin{description}
\item[* name:] TSubjOK
\item[* relevant examples:] \mbox{}\\
x1 walk \\
that he went away that surprises me
\item[* language:] (Dutch, English, Spanish) English
\item[* kind of rule:] (M-rule, S-rule, Transferrule) M-rule
\item[* subgrammar:] XPPROPtoCLAUSE
\item[* class:] (name of rule, transformation or filter class) TC\_ObjectOkrules
\item[* date of creation:] 18-MAR-1988
\item[* author:] margreet sanders
\item[* copied from:] Dutch TObjectOK0
\item[* modification:]\mbox{}
\begin{enumerate}
\item date: 28/9/88\ \ \ \ \ author: margreet sanders\\
Added: a condition on modalverbs: the CLAUSE received the thetavp of the 
embedded main verb, not of the modal, but also received the subject from the 
embedded sentence (see RModalComplSentSubst1 and 2). Therefore, all clauses 
containing a modal now have a subject, even if the embedded main verb is 
ergative.
\item date: ../../..\ \ \ \ \ author:
\end{enumerate}
\item[* task:] To let clauses that contain a subject, and no passive or
ergative non-caseassigning verbs, pass this TC.
\item[\ \ strategy:] (also: deviations from accepted proposals)
\item[\ \ rejected alternatives:]
\item[\ \ clarification of variables:]
\item[\ \ clarification of the splitting up into subrules:]dna
\item[\ \ clarification of the collapsing of rules:] (e.g. clarification of parameters)
\item[\ \ differences analytical/generative version:]none
\item[\  \ suggested semantics:]dna
\item[\ \ presuppositions:]\mbox{}
