\begin{verbatim}
% TRANSFORMATION TItSubjInsertion
< m1:CLAUSE{CLAUSErec1}
           [ I1:mu1,
             I2:mu2,
             predrel/VERBP{VERBPrec1}
                    [ mu3,
                      head/VERB{VERBrec1}[mu5],
                      mu4
                    ],
             mu7 
           ]
>

< m :CLAUSE{CLAUSErec1}
           [ I1:mu1,
             subjrel/NP{NPrec1}
                    [head/PERSPRO{PERSPROrec1}
                         [head/BPERSPRO(AUX_itBPERSPROkey){BPERSPROrec1}]
                    ],
             I2:mu2,
             predrel/VERBP{VERBPrec1}
                    [ mu3,
                      head/VERB{VERBrec1}[mu5],
                      mu4
                    ],
             mu7 
           ]
>

   MATCHCONDITIONS
      <
       I1: ALL (mu1, I11:rel1/..)
       I2: NOT EXIST (mu2, [ I11:rel1/..]) AND
           NOT EXIST (mu2, [subjrel/..])
          I11: rel1 IN AUX_presubjrels
       m1: ( EXIST (mu4, [complrel/I8::SENTENCE{SENTENCErec1}[mu8]]) 
             OR
             EXIST (mu7, [extraposrel/I8::SENTENCE{SENTENCErec1}[mu8]])
           ) 
           AND
           ( NOT EXIST (mu4, [I9:rel9/..])
             OR
             ( CLAUSErec1.voice = active AND 
               NOT CLAUSErec1.thetavp IN [vp010, vp012] )
           )
       m : ( EXIST (mu4, [complrel/I8::SENTENCE{SENTENCErec1}[mu8]]) 
             OR
             EXIST (mu7, [extraposrel/I8::SENTENCE{SENTENCErec1}[mu8]])
           ) 
           AND
           ( NOT EXIST (mu4, [I9:rel9/..]) 
             OR
             ( CLAUSErec1.voice = active AND 
               NOT CLAUSErec1.thetavp IN [vp010, vp012] )
           )
         I8: SENTENCErec1.PROsubject = true OR
             SENTENCErec1.finiteness = finite
         I9: rel9 IN [objrel,indobjrel]
>
      COMP
         <
          C1: true
          A1: NPrec1 := AUX_NPONitPRSPR
              (* including number = singular *)
         >
      DECOMP
         <
          C1: NPrec1 = AUX_NPONitPRSPR
          A1: @
         >

&

\end{verbatim}
\newpage
\begin{description}
\item[* name:] TItSubjInsertion
\item[* relevant examples:]\mbox{}
\begin{enumerate}
\item Active, non-ergative: Extraposition of subject (which is now complrel in 
VP, or extraposrel when coming from an XP):\\
-- do suprise me to see you there $\rightarrow$ It do surprise me to see you 
there\\
-- do be wrong to eat people $\rightarrow$ It do be wrong to eat people
\item Extraposition of object of ergatives:\\
-- had escaped me that you would be late $\rightarrow$ It had escaped me that 
you would be late
\item Passive, non-ergative, no object:\\
-- was discovered his colleagues had lied to him$\rightarrow$ It was 
discovered his colleagues had lied to him
\end{enumerate}
\item[* language:] (Dutch, English, Spanish) English
\item[* kind of rule:] (M-rule, S-rule, Transferrule) M-rule
\item[* subgrammar:]  XPPROPtoClause
\item[* class:] (name of rule, transformation or filter class) 
TC\_ObjectOKrules
\item[* date of creation:] 24-MAR-1988
\item[* author:] margreet sanders
\item[* copied from:] TThereSubjInsertion
\item[* modification:]\mbox{}
\begin{enumerate}
\item date: 17/05/89\ \ \ \ \ author: margreet sanders\\
Adapted rule to allow for non-ergative verbs (including {\em be\/}) with an 
object only if the clause is active (to prevent: It was forced them to swim)
\item date: 22/11/91\ \ \ \ \ author: petra de wit\\
adapted rule to allow for non-ergative verbs with an indirect object only if 
the clause is active (to prevent: It was asked them to leave). If revising of 
the patterns takes place and "ask" assigned the value DONP_OPENTOSENT, this 
adaption can be abolished.
\end{enumerate}
\item[* task:] To insert the dummy subject `it' when there is no subject and, 
in case of ergatives, no object. (But see modification above)
